@host = http://localhost:8080

### Login as alice (EMPLOYEE)
# @name alice
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username":"alice","password":"password123"}

### Login as bob (MANAGER)
# @name bob
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username":"bob","password":"password123"}

### Login as carol (FINANCE)
# @name carol
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username":"carol","password":"password123"}

### Login as dave (ADMIN)
# @name dave
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username":"dave","password":"password123"}

### Who am I? (alice)
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{alice.response.body.$.token}}

### Alice lists only her own expenses
GET {{host}}/api/expenses/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{alice.response.body.$.token}}

### Alice cannot list every expense -> 403
GET {{host}}/api/expenses
Authorization: Bearer {{alice.response.body.$.token}}

### Bob (MANAGER) can list every expense -> 200
GET {{host}}/api/expenses
Authorization: Bearer {{bob.response.body.$.token}}

### Alice creates a draft
# @name created
POST {{host}}/api/expenses
Authorization: Bearer {{alice.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"amount":25.50,"currency":"EUR","description":"Taxi home"}

### Alice submits her draft
POST {{host}}/api/expenses/{{created.response.body.$.id}}/submit
Authorization: Bearer {{alice.response.body.$.token}}

### Alice cannot approve her own claim -> 403
POST {{host}}/api/expenses/{{created.response.body.$.id}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{alice.response.body.$.token}}

### Bob approves the submitted claim -> 200
POST {{host}}/api/expenses/{{created.response.body.$.id}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{bob.response.body.$.token}}

### Bob cannot pay it (only FINANCE or ADMIN) -> 403
POST {{host}}/api/expenses/{{created.response.body.$.id}}/pay
Authorization: Bearer {{bob.response.body.$.token}}

### Carol pays the approved claim -> 200
POST {{host}}/api/expenses/{{created.response.body.$.id}}/pay
Authorization: Bearer {{carol.response.body.$.token}}

### Paying it again -> 409 Conflict
POST {{host}}/api/expenses/{{created.response.body.$.id}}/pay
Authorization: Bearer {{carol.response.body.$.token}}

### Bob can read but not edit alice's draft -> 403
PUT {{host}}/api/expenses/1
Authorization: Bearer {{bob.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"amount":1.00,"currency":"EUR","description":"Rewritten by a manager"}

### Alice edits her own draft -> 200
PUT {{host}}/api/expenses/2
Authorization: Bearer {{alice.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"amount":130.00,"currency":"EUR","description":"Team lunch (updated)"}

### Dave (ADMIN) lists users -> 200
GET {{host}}/api/admin/users
Authorization: Bearer {{dave.response.body.$.token}}

### Alice cannot list users -> 403
GET {{host}}/api/admin/users
Authorization: Bearer {{alice.response.body.$.token}}

### No token at all -> 401
GET {{host}}/api/expenses/mine
